.TH DANBY-LOGISTICPREY 1
.SH NAME
danby-logisticprey \- predator-prey model with logistic prey growth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/logisticprey
.SH MODEL
X' = rX(1-X/K)-aXY;
Y' = cXY-dY.
.PP
The prey population X is limited by carrying capacity K.  Predators Y grow by
converted predation and die at per-capita rate d.  When d/c<K, the positive
equilibrium is X=d/c and Y=r(1-X/K)/a.
.SH DISPLAY
The left panel is the phase portrait with the analytic equilibrium marked.
The right panel shows both population histories.  Unlike the neutral closed
orbits of the Volterra model, logistic regulation can attract trajectories.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the phase portrait to set initial populations and the bottom tracks to
set r, K, a, c, and d.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/logisticprey.b
.br
.B /appl/danby/logisticprey.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-ecology (1),
.IR numerics (2)
